A||N||15||RoadRocket||Cursed Gas Guage!||||8||
Z||000000||RoadRocket||10-07-2001||10:27 PM||||Damn near did it to me again! I was cruising down the road, showed I had a quarter tank and only 260 miles after my last refuel, when I started to run out of gas! I used to see at least 300 miles before I had to worry about getting gas!<P>The last two times it did that to me, I was (1) in a snow storm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> and (2) in a rainstorm with the flu!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>It's bad enough my fuel mileage is dropping, this only makes it worse!<P>I remember reading either here or on A.A.Fiero that all you need to do is clean the sending unit (the electronics, rather) and that fixes the problem. Requires dropping the tank, though.<P>What's the procedure for it? Anyone got it listed somewhere? I don't have the time or facilities to do it, but maybe if I can take it to a mechanic, I can get them to do it for me.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||8
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-07-2001||10:38 PM||||Dunno what the fix is, but Ive got the same problem in my Formula...runs empty when it shows 1/4 tank (now I never let it get below half tank).....and like you, I learned the hard way!<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gerald||10-07-2001||11:01 PM||||I was under my fiero today and i think that doing the tank on the ground wouldnt be too bad. Just need some jack stands and a friend.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ray b||10-07-2001||11:21 PM||||NO DONOT DROP TANK<BR>FIRST FILL IT UP AND SEE WHERE THE GAUGE IS POINTING  OVER PASSED FULL MARK????<BR>the gauge pointer is lose on the shaft<BR>the pointer is just pressed on<BR>remove the cover and grab it by the center hub and pull it off.<BR> fill tank to the max all the way full not first click off then reinstall it lined up with the full mark I glue mine with super glue.<BR>NOW IT IS INDEXED AND WILL READ E WHEN EMPTY<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||10-07-2001||11:49 PM||||<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Dunno what the fix is, but Ive got the same problem in my Formula...runs empty when it shows 1/4 tank (now I never let it get below half tank).....and like you, I learned the hard way!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>My 88gt is the same way. After I filled it the first time I let it get to 1/4 tank. Thankfully, it will run like hell first before it runs out completely. I was only 50 yards or so from a station and it took over 11.5 gallons to fill it. The tank is the 11.9 gallon, so I was real close. <P>I don't let it fall below 1/2 tank either. <BR>You fill up more often but spend less time at the pump. <BR>My car appreciates a full tank anyway. In the situation I described above, the fuel pump was wailing like a banshee trying to feed the V6. Engine runs much smoother at or near a full tank anyhow.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||ray b||10-08-2001||01:13 AM||||banshee screams are a death sound of the pump run it dry and it will fail soon.<BR>then you will need to drop the tank and too much $$$ to the dealer.<BR>try to check you gauge if it is over the F full mark when toped off it will be off on E tooo and run out at 1/4 to 1/2 mark MOVE IT TO MATCH THE FULL LINE [NOT OVER IT} THEN IT WILL READ E WHEN EMPTY<BR>I HAVE DONE 3 CARS NOW ALL WORK GOOD, CHEAP TOO.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||11
Z||000006||WampusCat||10-08-2001||07:28 AM||||Mine does't go over the F when full but still runs out at 1/4 tank.  Must be at the sender end instead of the guage.||||reg||1
Z||000007||grinthock||10-08-2001||08:01 AM||||Mine does the same thing guys, but one other problem.<P>It started showing WAY WAY over F and shows empty at 1/4 as well, but it also wavers.  Like if I am driving and I accelerate HARD the pin goes all the way to F and stays there until I brake, then if I brake pretty good the pin FLYS back down to the right spot<P>That's a loose pin????||||reg||1
Z||000008||falconhulk||10-08-2001||08:10 AM||||Got a related question....was there ever a 8 gallon tank?  I have a 85 se v6 and I thought the guage was off.  I ran about 160 miles and the needle was on empty.  I was going to stop at a station that was on my way and about 200 feet up the road after driving 100 miles.  All of a sudden I lost all power.  I let off the gas thinking I was out.  The car did not die and I was able to get to the station and fill up.  It took 8.1 gallons.  I thought I had a 10 gallon tank.  I got a total of 160 miles out of that tank of gas.  Thats about 20 mpg and not bad as I was doing about 85 the entire way.    <p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pheagey||10-08-2001||09:05 AM||||dude I know how you feel. My '88 coupe had the same problem. Ran soem fuel systems clean througth it and repositioned the needle on the gauge. At full it reads 7/8 tank and empty is under the E. <BR>Good luck. <A HREF="Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html" TARGET=_blank>Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||ray b||10-08-2001||01:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Mine does the same thing guys, but one other problem.<P>It started showing WAY WAY over F and shows empty at 1/4 as well, but it also wavers.  Like if I am driving and I accelerate HARD the pin goes all the way to F and stays there until I brake, then if I brake pretty good the pin FLYS back down to the right spot<P>That's a loose pin????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the over reading is a lose shifted pin ,<BR>the movement is normal on hard brake or acc.<BR>but it is all so sticking from gum or varnish deposits on the float meck in the tank gas condishioner may help or remove the sender with the fuel pump and use a gumout type cleaner or get a junkyard replacement.<BR>G M DEALER wanted $450 for a new sender rig so thats not a real way to go.<BR>try to move the gauge pin and old gas condishener first, droping the tank is no fun <P><P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000011||Rodrv6||10-08-2001||03:52 PM||||Falconhulk,<BR>I feel your pain.  The smallest tank in the Fiero was the 10.6 gallon one in the early cars.  However, due to their design, the gas station pump nozzle will shut off about 2 or 3 gallons before the tank is actually full  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>For many years now I've been patiently dribbling in the last couple of gallons until the tank is really full.  My 84 would hold 3 gallons more after shutoff, my 88 will hold 2.<BR>I've never had any problems doing this--the vapor canister has never loaded up or anything--it's just a real pain.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000012||RoadRocket||10-08-2001||09:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>fill tank to the max all the way full not first click off then reinstall it lined up with the full mark I glue mine with super glue.<BR>NOW IT IS INDEXED AND WILL READ E WHEN EMPTY<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Whenever I fill the tank, it shows just above the full line, not 1/4 above the full line. So I'm not inclined to think that's the problem.<P>That being said, however, Rod points out that the Fiero tank causes the pumps to snap off before it is completely full, so maybe this is , in fact, my problem.<P>Go figure...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000013||RoadRocket||10-08-2001||09:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodrv6:<BR><B>However, due to their design, the gas station pump nozzle will shut off about 2 or 3 gallons before the tank is actually full   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Damn! This may actually be my problem! When it ran out of gas the other day, I only filled it up to 10.5 gallons! I have an 88, and had forgotten that they have a twelve gallon tank! <P>In the past, I would top of the tank without thinking about it. I haven't done it since I brought the car out of retirement. So it may very well be a combination of both problems!<P>Looks like I'm gonna have to try both yours and Ray's suggestions.<P>Thanks to the both of you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000014||JohnF||10-09-2001||08:45 AM||||My '88 also runs out of gas at 1/4 tank.  It started this at about 70K or so (and left me stranded 2 blocks from home).  Now, I fill up at about 1/2 tank and remember what I was told long ago, "It costs the same to keep the top half of the tank filled as it does the bottom half!".<P>Re-indexing needle seems like a neat fix.  I'm doing it!||||reg||1
Z||000015||ray b||10-09-2001||01:33 PM||||make sure you are all the way full to the maxthis will take some time and many clicks on the gas pump look in the manual for your cars tank size, or you can set the pointer to under read [less than full line and have a reserve at E line] depends on your stile and tastes.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
